UID:9SpIddUd5v
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 98 mins (1h38m)\n\nIn 1987\, at the age of just 21\,
  Marlee Matlin shattered expectations as the first Deaf actor to win an Ac
 ademy Award® for her groundbreaking performance in Children of a Lesser G
 od. Catapulted into the spotlight\, she seized the moment to challenge an 
 industry unprepared for her immense talent\, emerging as a trailblazer not
  only as a performer but also as an author and activist. All screenings w
 ill be presented with Open Captions.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-the
 aters/marlee-matlin
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
